 the open world and in  the traditional dark souls style legacy  dungeons it [ __ ] hits but if you have  never played a souls game and want to  know if you should try elden ring or if  you did play souls games didn't like  them and now you're feeling some intense  fomo because everyone on your steam list  is 40 hours into their adventure in the  lands between  let me try to sell you on the game a  little bit so to start if you like just  the idea of a challenging action rpg  that doesn't really hold your hand  i think you should just check out elden  ring without asking any more questions  there is a real satisfaction from  triumphing over this game's challenges  to go back to the challenge thing elden  ring respects your intelligence and  skill as a player and it's not going to  throw stuff at you that's impossible but  it's also not going to throw anything  super easy at you nothing feels as good  as triumphing over this game's  challenges and in terms of the open  world elden ring doesn't have any  waypoints or quest markers or really  many collectibles beyond important items  weapons and crafting materials this is  not a game that is telling you where to  go or what to do basically at any time  in that way it's really different from  modern open world action games like  assassin's creed or far cry those games  are often defined by checklist of chores  that the devs think you might enjoy  doing while playing the game elden ring  pretty much leaves all that decision  making up to you and whatever you see on  the horizon that might look cool to  explore in that way it's a lot like  breath of the wild another truly  incredible open world game that left all  the content finding and path making up  to you as the player it's really good  stuff for example i really struggled  with the game's first story boss so i  explored the open world instead of  bashing my head against him some more  that way i ended up going into an area  that was leading to one of the game's  end game zones and my level 20 ass was  pushing up against level 50 content and  doing mostly fine by playing smart and  using all the cool tools i was picking  up another awesome moment i had in the  open world was actually in that near  endgame zone i was wandering around i  saw a windmill and a bunch of women  dancing around a bonfire near it i  approached because i saw an item in the  bonfire and it was actually the  nobleman's armor set these ladies were  burning a rich dude alive and as soon as  i pulled his clothes and weapon out of  the fire their eyes turned red they  pulled out pitchforks and torches and  they started attacking me not only that  but a bunch of burning skeletons rose up  from the bonfire and started attacking  me too specifically by exploding at me  for huge damage it was a really cool  moment my last little cool moment that  i'll share with you that hopefully  convinces you that this game is really  something special and worth trying is a  cheese strap i found that is really  really cool i ended up being a level 50  character in a level 80 near endgame  zone because i killed a boss using the  rot status ailment i inflicted him with  rot and then walked away as the poison  slowly killed him i had no business  meeting this boss and yet i did it  because this game really lets you do  anything you want and before you worry  that all this fun freely exploration  gets ruined by how hard everyone says  this game is i'm here to tell you that  eldon ring does not have to be that  difficult if you don't want it to be  there are a lot of invisible difficulty  switches you can flip if you want to  make the game easier for you and you  shouldn't let anyone tell you that  you're playing the game wrong for using  them so now that you hopefully agree  with me that elden ring is a really cool  game that you should check out because  it's so unique and interesting and fun  let me share some tips with you on how  to make the play experience a little  less bumpy as you're starting out  starting out with the fact that there is  a secret tutorial right here jump down  this hole i promise i know it looks  deadly but there is a tutorial down  there it'll teach you all about combat  including all the new things added to  this game the previous from soft games  didn't have like guard counters for  example before you go into tutorial  though you'll have to pick a class you  can't really go wrong here but you  definitely shouldn't pick wretch it's  really hard for a new player meanwhile  samurai and astrologer are really great  choices for a first timer as for  keepsakes mostly two options for a  beginner golden seed if you want extra  heals or fanged imp ashes if you want a  bit of an easier time fighting bosses  now once you've done all that the most  important thing you can do is follow the  golden arrows on your map leading from  sight of grace to sight of grace i  believe once you hit for them you'll  meet molina who is going to give you a  horse which is very important and teach  you how to level up from there you could  go to fight the first main boss margaret  i'm not ashamed to tell you i didn't  beat him until i was level 23. he is  hard instead of bashing your head  against him you should do some exploring  there's lots of stuff to do in limb  grave and you will get lots of levels  while doing it you can actually go and  do the entire second main dungeon before  beating market and honestly i kind of  think that dungeon is easier so maybe  it's a good choice speaking of exploring  the first and most important thing you  should be doing in any area in the game  is getting the map fragment the first  one is right here but if you open your  map after entering a new area you can  actually see where the map fragment is  hanging out eldering puts a lot of stuff  directly on the map so make sure to keep  checking it and the last tip i can give  you is to please use summons and ashes  of war when you need them they will make  bosses easier if you're having trouble  and it is not wrong to make use of that  i know lots of people will say that  using these mechanics isn't playing the  game as intended but [ __ ] those people  do whatever you need to do to make this  game fun for you that's what playing  games is about anyway i think eldon ring  is a fantastic game and if you've made  it all the way to the end of this video  i think you'll enjoy it too it is really  cool and unique and it lets you play  however you want it is not as daunting  as some people say it is if that's  what's scaring you off plus no other  game has a turtle pope gonna look at  this dude he's awesome  the weirdest thing that happened to me  is that so there's a lot of churches  around the game that are churches like  it's a very i assume to like various  deities in the game's mythology  there's a lot of george rr martin ass  [ __ ] in here one of them is the church  of irit i-r-i-t-h which is my mom's name  and she spells it really specifically  with the th even because it's just like  kind of close to the way that you might  spell it in hebrew and  that's exactly like that in this game  and it really threw me off i had to send  her a picture it [ __ ] me up it was so  weird

